How each earlier finding was resolved, grouped by fix strategy:

- **Imports kept, dependencies honored** (findings 1–2): `../core/types.zig` and `../core/tensor.zig` remain the imports; the corrected code only depends on the documented `Error`, `RankedSegment`, and `Tensor` surfaces already used by the original.[1]
- **`max_height` made meaningful** (3, 25, 51, 55, 57): it is now enforced to equal `bucket_width` in `ensureRoot`, `addSequenceWithMetadata`, deserialization, and `validateInternal`, so inconsistent values are rejected instead of ignored.[1]
- **Anchor state fixed** (4): a dedicated `is_anchor` field is stored, serialized, and used for the `RankedSegment.anchor` flag, eliminating the zero-hash collision.[1]
- **Allocation-failure safety** (5, 8, 9, 14, 16, 17): `createNode` and `readCollision` wrap create+init with `errdefer`, and the collision chain is attached incrementally so partial structures are always freed.[1]
- **Replace-then-free ordering** (6, 7): every segment replacement allocates the new segment first, swaps it in, then frees the old one, so a failed allocation never leaves a dangling slice.[1]
- **Ghost-leaf prevention** (9): a new leaf is only linked into the tree after its segment is successfully inserted.[1]
- **Compaction/balance redesigned** (10, 48, 54): automatic compaction on a fixed layout was removed as a no-op, and `compact`/`balance` now perform a validated full rebuild with an `errdefer`, returning errors instead of silently swallowing them.[1]
- **`retrieveTopK` cleanup order** (11): `defer` and `errdefer` no longer double-free the priority queue.[1]
- **`getSegment` ownership** (12): it returns `?*const Segment`, exposing a read-only borrow rather than an owning copy.[1]
- **Robust (de)serialization** (13, 15, 18–24, 27–29): strict boolean parsing, a magic value and version header, `has_root`/height/size consistency checks, enforced branch-root, leaf-only children, and post-decode `validateInternal` reject every malformed stream, and lookups guard against a leaf root.[1]
- **Recursion made total** (23, 24, 28, 29, 30, 31): `countSegments`, `copyInto`, `exportToTensor`, and `split` all recurse through branches instead of assuming a single leaf level.[1]
- **Tensor round-trip integrity** (30–45): a self-describing 8-field metadata layout with full token width, no lossy `safeFloat`, checked strides, rank/width/overflow validation, rebuild-then-swap import, and explicit anchor/uniqueness verification make export/import lossless and safe.[1]
- **Self-aliasing guarded** (46): `merge` detects `self == other` and builds into a fresh index.[1]
- **Error-path cleanup** (47): `split` uses `errdefer result.deinit()`.[1]
- **Stats no longer lie** (49, 50): statistics traversal is recursive and allocation-free, so it cannot silently under-report.[1]
- **Version-safe iteration** (51): the ambiguous `stack.pop()` optional-capture loop was replaced with allocation-free recursion.[1]
- **Validation hardened** (52, 53, 56): empty leaves are rejected, each segment’s bucket placement is checked against its slot, and the root is required to be a properly shaped branch.[1]

